  "section_notes": "S2 was softened so that exceeding the 5% limit triggers only corrective action and regulator review, not a sales stop. That is a weakening that benefits Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2% failure). S1, S3 (12 months for new units, 72 months retrofit), S4 (36 months) and S5 (8 per 100k, mandatory recall) fall within safe or acceptable ranges. Per-model results go to customers and regulators but not to the public, so the red lines are respected."
